      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Wednesday, October 12, 2005 The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-759",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64aa8b749be84711c2fac91dbb619cf9b7f201e534a440e485d5de170303ea9d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64aa8b749be8-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Federal Tort Claims Act waives the sovereign immunity of the United States for the torts of Federal employees when private persons in like circumstances would be liable. But instead of applying private-person principles of liability, the Ninth Circuit looked to the State and governmental-entity principles of liability."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-04-759",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64aa8b749be84711c2fac91dbb619cf9b7f201e534a440e485d5de170303ea9d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64aa8b749be8-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Do I understand that you would accept the rule that if Arizona held a private inspector liable to third persons for their injuries, then the Government of the United States would be liable?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-04-759",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64aa8b749be84711c2fac91dbb619cf9b7f201e534a440e485d5de170303ea9d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64aa8b749be8-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There was an argument that was made in your brief, and I didn't fully grasp the thrust of it, in the -- that is, you said that the Mine Safety and Health Administration has a duty to the Secretary of Labor, but not to the mine operator and not to the miner. If that were true, then would there be -- you wouldn't even get to the Good Samaritan doctrine, would you, if the only duty is to the Secretary of Labor?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Maynard",
      "case_id": "2005-04-759",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64aa8b749be84711c2fac91dbb619cf9b7f201e534a440e485d5de170303ea9d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64aa8b749be8-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think there is an argument that we are not rendering services to another."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-759",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64aa8b749be84711c2fac91dbb619cf9b7f201e534a440e485d5de170303ea9d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64aa8b749be8-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do we have to decide what the Arizona rule is in order to decide the main question presented -- namely, whether the analogy to Arizona public officials is sufficient?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-04-759",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64aa8b749be84711c2fac91dbb619cf9b7f201e534a440e485d5de170303ea9d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64aa8b749be8-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's just a background question. I'm curious, was ASARCO sued here, or -- and is its liability capped by workmen's comp laws, or?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cotter",
      "case_id": "2005-04-759",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64aa8b749be84711c2fac91dbb619cf9b7f201e534a440e485d5de170303ea9d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64aa8b749be8-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Thank you, Your Honor. Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: I'd like to begin by addressing the last point made by the Office of the Solicitor General, which is the Daggett case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2005-04-759",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64aa8b749be84711c2fac91dbb619cf9b7f201e534a440e485d5de170303ea9d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64aa8b749be8-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: That's actually a rather interesting question I don't really know the answer to."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-759",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64aa8b749be84711c2fac91dbb619cf9b7f201e534a440e485d5de170303ea9d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64aa8b749be8-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What was your response to the motion to dismiss?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-759",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64aa8b749be84711c2fac91dbb619cf9b7f201e534a440e485d5de170303ea9d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64aa8b749be8-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. COTTER: And what happened was, frankly, Judge Browning dismissed, relying, I think, on the -- more on the discretionary function exception"
    }
